# BundleCodeBase.ps1 output (repo-bundle text for agy upload)
/clavity.txt

# NOTE: .NET build-output rules ([Bb]in/, [Oo]bj/, artifacts/, *.user) moved to
# clavity-dotnet/.gitignore during the monorepo consolidation. They were UNANCHORED
# here and leaked into the Rust tools' src/bin/ dirs, silently dropping real binary
# targets (e.g. clavity-classic/src/bin/fake_tmux.rs). Each product folder now owns
# its own build-output ignore rules.

# Internal design provenance — excluded from the PUBLIC repo (kept locally, untracked).
# Pre-push audit WS2 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-pre-push-audit-design.md): these hold
# in-flight TBDs, superseded-model narratives, and local-machine paths not fit for public.
# DEFAULT-DENY with opt-IN exceptions. Everything here stays excluded unless a negation below names it,
# because 15 of these files carry local machine paths. Add a negation only after reading the file and
# confirming it is public-safe — no local paths, no in-flight TBDs, no superseded narratives.
#
# Why this is written as three lines per level instead of a single `docs/superpowers/` rule: git does not
# descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a negation can never resurrect a file beneath one. Each level
# must therefore exclude its *contents* (`dir/*`) while leaving the directory itself traversable, and
# re-admit the next level explicitly. Changing these back to a bare `docs/superpowers/` silently breaks
# every negation below without any error.
docs/superpowers/*
!docs/superpowers/specs/
docs/superpowers/specs/*
!docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-21-golden-header-epic-sequencing-design.md
!docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-ship-agy-disciplines-design.md
!docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-docs-rationalize-tool-design.md
# Implementation plans — same DEFAULT-DENY opt-IN discipline as specs above: re-admit the plans/
# directory, exclude its contents, then negate each public-safe plan file by name after reading it.
!docs/superpowers/plans/
docs/superpowers/plans/*
!docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-22-docs-rationalize-sp1-user-facing-list.md
!docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-22-docs-rationalize-sp2-audit-script.md
docs/session-notes/
.clavity/

# docs-rationalize audit tool (SP2) — per-run generated working artifacts (owner ruling: gitignored).
# Regenerated on every `just docs-audit`; never committed, never user-facing.
docs/docs-audit-findings.json
docs/docs-audit-findings.md
docs/docs-audit-log.md
docs/docs-audit.lock

# Secret-shaped / junk guards (defense-in-depth — no secret is tracked today, keep it that way)
*.pem
*.key
*.log
.env.local
.DS_Store

# Scratch dumps
diff.txt

# Pester -CI output (regenerated by `just test-scripts` / the release pre-flight each run)
testResults.xml

# PowerShell's module-analysis cache (Microsoft/Windows/PowerShell/ModuleAnalysisCache). Lands in the
# repo root when a script runs with LOCALAPPDATA/USERPROFILE redirected here — the sandboxed installer /
# registrar tests do exactly that. Regenerated on demand; safe to delete. ANCHORED with a leading slash
# so it can only ever mean this one root-level dir (see the .NET build-output note above for what an
# unanchored rule cost us).
/Microsoft/
